-- §6  The residue's three points, whether they came back in order, and whether the demand crossed a tooth.
# One row per lumpy corpus layer with a stated demand, carrying the demand's three points, the
# quantum's, whether the residue evaluated at those points comes back ordered, and whether the
# demand range crosses a multiple of the quantum.
#
# Two parts of a remainder
#   `r = mq - (d mod q)` splits a remainder into a part a procurement decision moves and a part no
#   decision removes. The second half is a sawtooth in `d`, so evaluated at an interval's three
#   points it need not come back ordered, and an unordered triple is not a valid interval at all,
#   while the demand it was computed from is perfectly well formed.
#
# The tooth is the census, the order is a symptom
#   A demand inside one tooth always gives ordered residues; one that crosses need not, and may
#   still come back ordered by luck, as `(0.2, 1.5, 2.7)` with `q = 1` does. So `crosses_tooth` is
#   what makes the split unfilable and `sawtoothed` is what a reader would see. Proof:
#   `src/proofs/README.md`, entry `sawtooth`.
#
# Calculated twice, not counted by hand
#   The example recomputes every `mod` and every floor in Rust and asserts both verdicts match
#   these columns.
#
# `quantum_mode` alone is the divisor
#   Because every filed quantum in this corpus is a point value. The example asserts that rather
#   than assuming it: a quantum with a spread would make "the residue" three different divisions
#   and this query would be picking one silently.
#
# Corpus only
#   The fixtures exist to exercise states the corpus does not reach, so counting them here would
#   report coverage this model has not actually been filed against.
-- layers/lumpy.sqlc at corpus scope; the sawtooth is mod(d, q) at the three points.
SELECT l.filing               AS "filing!",
       l.layer                AS "layer!",
       l.d_low::float8        AS "d_low!",
       l.d_mode::float8       AS "d_mode!",
       l.d_high::float8       AS "d_high!",
       l.quantum_low::float8  AS "q_low!",
       l.quantum_mode::float8 AS "q_mode!",
       l.quantum_high::float8 AS "q_high!",
       (NOT (mod(l.d_low,  l.quantum_mode) <= mod(l.d_mode, l.quantum_mode)
         AND mod(l.d_mode, l.quantum_mode) <= mod(l.d_high, l.quantum_mode)))
                              AS "sawtoothed!",
       (floor(l.d_low / l.quantum_mode) <> floor(l.d_high / l.quantum_mode))
                              AS "crosses_tooth!"
FROM (
    :compose(layers/lumpy.sqlc)
) l
JOIN (
    :compose(scope/corpus.sqlc)
) f USING (filing)
WHERE l.d_low IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY l.filing, l.layer
